Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 18:13:49 2026 +1100

    nova: Precheck for a host virtlogd
    
    nova_libvirt runs its own virtlogd and shares the host's /run, so a
    virtlogd running or enabled on the host conflicts with it and, with
    older images, makes instance creation fail as libvirt sends console
    logs to a virtlogd that cannot see the instance directories.
    
    Fail prechecks when the host's virtlogd units are active or enabled.
    Unlike the host libvirt check, run this on existing deployments too,
    since the conflict only matters once console logs go via virtlogd.
    
    Prompt: interactive debugging of an upgrade error report from ``Vii``
    on the #openstack-kolla IRC channel.
    
    Related-Bug: #2155214
    Change-Id: Iabecbda82f1676f0b551b10efc80e5c35d68e0d0
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

diff --git a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/precheck.yml b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/precheck.yml
index b61d2292c..8035a30a6 100644
--- a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/precheck.yml
+++ b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/precheck.yml
@@ -134,6 +134,32 @@
     - container_facts.containers['nova_libvirt'] is not defined
     - service | service_enabled_and_mapped_to_host
 
+- name: Host virtlogd checks
+  vars:
+    service: "{{ nova_cell_services['nova-libvirt'] }}"
+  when:
+    - service | service_enabled_and_mapped_to_host
+  block:
+    - name: Get state of host virtlogd units  # noqa command-instead-of-module
+      become: true
+      ansible.builtin.command:
+        cmd: "systemctl show --property ActiveState,UnitFileState virtlogd.socket virtlogd.service"
+      register: host_virtlogd
+      changed_when: false
+      check_mode: false
+
+    - name: Checking that host virtlogd is not running or enabled
+      ansible.builtin.fail:
+        msg: >-
+          virtlogd is running or enabled on the host. The nova_libvirt
+          container runs its own virtlogd, and shares /run with the host, so
+          a host virtlogd will prevent nova_libvirt from starting. Stop and
+          disable the host virtlogd.socket, virtlogd-admin.socket and
+          virtlogd.service units.
+      when: >-
+        'ActiveState=active' in host_virtlogd.stdout_lines or
+        'UnitFileState=enabled' in host_virtlogd.stdout_lines
+
 - name: Checking that nova_libvirt container is not running
   vars:
     nova_libvirt: "{{ nova_cell_services['nova-libvirt'] }}"
diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/nova-libvirt-host-virtlogd-precheck-5d2a8e7c1f9b3a64.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/nova-libvirt-host-virtlogd-precheck-5d2a8e7c1f9b3a64.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..616ff0cb1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/nova-libvirt-host-virtlogd-precheck-5d2a8e7c1f9b3a64.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    A precheck now fails if ``virtlogd`` is running or enabled on a compute
+    host. The ``nova_libvirt`` container runs its own ``virtlogd`` and
+    shares ``/run`` with the host, so a host ``virtlogd`` either prevents
+    the container from starting or, with older images, causes instance
+    creation to fail with ``Unable to open file:
+    /var/lib/nova/instances/<uuid>/console.log``. Stop and disable the
+    host's ``virtlogd.socket``, ``virtlogd-admin.socket`` and
+    ``virtlogd.service`` units before upgrading.
